{
  "chapter.681B4DB073FB10D5.title": "01 • MineColonies: A Living Colony",
  "task.3B7BB3BD7EFFB0B3.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.59C2E82B3B2557C7.title": "Start here: MineColonies",
  "quest.59C2E82B3B2557C7.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.59C2E82B3B2557C7.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "MineColonies turns a base into a working settlement. Citizens build blueprints, gather materials, cook, deliver supplies and research upgrades. You manage jobs and requests rather than placing every building block yourself. StyleColonies adds architectural choices to the build system.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Your route: site and supplies -> Town Hall and builder -> housing and food -> warehouse and couriers -> production, research and defense -> a self-supplied expansion.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Read the next guide card before building. This chapter teaches working setups; it does not replace JEI recipes or the mod's own manual."
  ],
  "task.1798041B47F38631.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.55EDA03B1FB4A0D6.title": "How to use this guide",
  "quest.55EDA03B1FB4A0D6.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.55EDA03B1FB4A0D6.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Arrows suggest a learning order. Item tasks check what you carry; a checkmark is your own confirmation of a practical step. Neither is proof that an entire machine or colony works.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Open a quest, read Why / Do / Tip, then click its item to inspect it in JEI. R shows recipes and U shows uses with the default bindings. Read ahead, complete the described experiment, and only then tick practical tasks. Items are not consumed.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use JEI for this pack's quantities and substitutions. Pick a small test area and keep outputs visible. Existing equipment can count; briefly pick it up only when safe. Troubleshooting and a final project are at the end."
  ],
  "task.40521F65525C7D15.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.40376CAADCA40739.title": "Choose land and a style",
  "quest.40376CAADCA40739.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.40376CAADCA40739.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A colony needs room for future buildings, paths and changing elevations. A beautiful first house is less useful if every later blueprint overlaps a mountain.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Scout a broad area near materials. Preview the style you want with the Build Tool, including higher building levels, before committing. Plan a central storage area and leave walking space between entrances.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "StyleColonies supplies styles, not a second colony system. Large styles can require unusual decorative materials; inspect the preview and resource list first."
  ],
  "task.662ADB40F6532F72.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.71ADC4A26B994969.title": "A supply camp or ship",
  "quest.71ADC4A26B994969.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.71ADC4A26B994969.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The supply structure gives you a starter shelter and colony equipment. It is a starting kit, not an operating colony.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Use a Supply Camp on suitable land, or choose the Supply Ship alternative in JEI. Resolve the highlighted placement obstructions, place the structure, and collect its Town Hall and Build Tool.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Choose either structure; this checklist accepts both routes. Do not place a second supply structure just for this guide."
  ],
  "task.072E1C7622F3D5F3.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.7BC3A2AC07F7B091.title": "Found your settlement",
  "quest.7BC3A2AC07F7B091.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.7BC3A2AC07F7B091.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Town Hall establishes the colony and gives access to citizen, work and permission management.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Place the Town Hall with the Build Tool at your planned center. Open it, establish/name the colony and inspect its information. Keep the area reachable by ordinary walking paths.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Placing a hut block and completing its building are different steps. Do not assume the blueprint has already been built."
  ],
  "task.2D3016661DBDBA7A.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.6DCD38F81AE6889F.title": "Your first builder",
  "quest.6DCD38F81AE6889F.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.6DCD38F81AE6889F.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A builder constructs and upgrades the colony. Without one, a queue of hut blocks is only a queue of plans.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Place a Builder's Hut blueprint with the Build Tool. Assign an available citizen if necessary, request its construction, and open the hut to inspect the active job and required resources.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "The builder can build their own initial hut. Queue one small project first so you learn the request system before expanding."
  ],
  "task.20A6328863326D41.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.5CE76239A3358618.title": "Read the request list",
  "quest.5CE76239A3358618.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.5CE76239A3358618.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Most stalled jobs are a specific missing item, tool or condition. The Clipboard helps you see colony requests instead of guessing.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Read the builder's request, supply the exact requested material or a permitted substitution, then watch work resume. Use the hut resource interface and Clipboard to locate the next bottleneck.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "A similar-looking block from another mod may not be accepted. The request tells you which item is needed."
  ],
  "task.789FE9B5023ED13F.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.61C01C6EB265C963.title": "Keep workers fed",
  "quest.61C01C6EB265C963.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.61C01C6EB265C963.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Hungry citizens stop being productive. A Dining Hall distributes meals; the Chef's Kitchen is a separate production building.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build and staff a Dining Hall. Initially supply acceptable prepared food yourself and check that citizens can reach it and eat. Automate food production after this basic delivery loop works.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "A worker with food problems needs food access, not another task in their queue. Check citizen status messages first."
  ],
  "task.310E33F64326FBFA.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.58F86761CC305FCA.title": "Housing and happiness",
  "quest.58F86761CC305FCA.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.58F86761CC305FCA.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Residences provide stable housing and support population growth. More people require food, jobs and beds, not just recruitment.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a Residence and inspect assignments. Check citizen happiness, access to shelter and basic needs before recruiting more workers.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Upgrade housing as your settlement grows. Avoid expanding population faster than your food supply and builders can support."
  ],
  "task.581D5E484F8DFBFC.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.082E6F2C61EF913B.title": "A reliable wood supply",
  "quest.082E6F2C61EF913B.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.082E6F2C61EF913B.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Building consumes large amounts of wood. A Forester can turn an accessible planting area into a renewable supply.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build and staff the Forester's Hut. Supply the requested tool and saplings, check its work area, and confirm logs arrive in its inventory.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Keep decorative trees outside the selected work zone. Watch one full planting/harvesting cycle before depending on the output."
  ],
  "task.2B4CE46E6CBCAD74.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.2A3B0630147CC528.title": "Storage with a purpose",
  "quest.2A3B0630147CC528.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.2A3B0630147CC528.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Warehouse is the colony's shared store. It supports requests and crafting; an unrelated chest or RS disk is not automatically part of it.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a Warehouse and stock it with common building materials. Inspect its racks and capacity, and keep access routes clear.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use colony-aware storage and delivery paths. Moving supplies into a warehouse is only half the system; couriers perform deliveries."
  ],
  "task.3A7962CE16538B8F.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.302E3FA9C8C56751.title": "Connect the supply chain",
  "quest.302E3FA9C8C56751.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.302E3FA9C8C56751.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Couriers move requested supplies between the warehouse and workplaces, removing much of your manual delivery work.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build and staff a Courier's Hut. Trigger a small builder request using material already in the warehouse, then observe the courier delivering it.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "If delivery stalls, check path access, courier availability, warehouse space and whether the exact item is stocked."
  ],
  "task.578044AF1711F7EF.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.41054430E156DC83.title": "Turn crops into meals",
  "quest.41054430E156DC83.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.41054430E156DC83.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A Farm provides ingredients; a complete food chain also needs cooking and delivery.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a Farm, configure its fields, provide seeds and tools, and observe a harvest. Route ingredients toward the relevant cooking workplace and keep meals available at the Dining Hall.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not empty every seed into a machine. Keep planting reserves and verify the crop type in the field setup."
  ],
  "task.405FAD816EBDC3DC.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.29940787C35F8C0A.title": "Teach the sawmill",
  "quest.29940787C35F8C0A.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.29940787C35F8C0A.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A colony cannot fulfill a crafted-block request unless a suitable worker knows the recipe and has ingredients.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build and staff a Sawmill. Teach a simple supported wooden recipe, stock its inputs, and request that product through a building job.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Recipe capacity and available recipes depend on building level and research. Test one recipe before teaching an entire style palette."
  ],
  "task.5382EBCDBF41CBCA.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.0DEF901F188B8E8D.title": "Stone and tools",
  "quest.0DEF901F188B8E8D.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.0DEF901F188B8E8D.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A Stonemason and later a Blacksmith help close the gap between raw resources and construction requests.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Add a Stonemason, teach a needed stone recipe and test it. Plan a Blacksmith for suitable tools and metal products as its research/build requirements become available.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Follow a request backward: final block -> crafter recipe -> ingredient supply -> courier. This reveals which link is actually missing."
  ],
  "task.311F5C88EA092A09.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.325942E4FB3ECE8D.title": "Research with a reason",
  "quest.325942E4FB3ECE8D.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.325942E4FB3ECE8D.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Research unlocks buildings and improvements. Its prerequisites are part of colony progression, not a problem to bypass by crafting a hut early.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a University when its requirements are met, assign a researcher, and select a research that solves a current need. Supply the requested materials and inspect the prerequisites and duration.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Choose a useful unlock before chasing every branch. Keep the colony loaded for work to progress under your pack's chunk-loading rules."
  ],
  "task.1FD8742FE8DE0365.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.43F029CD893A6FF1.title": "Upgrade your capacity",
  "quest.43F029CD893A6FF1.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.43F029CD893A6FF1.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Upgrading the builder expands what they can construct. Higher-level workplaces also improve capabilities, storage and recipes.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Read the next upgrade's material list and builder-level requirement. Upgrade the Builder's Hut when needed, then upgrade one bottleneck workplace and verify the benefit.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not schedule every upgrade simultaneously. Preserve tools, food and access while your main builder is occupied."
  ],
  "task.419FB675F6DBA4A1.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.3FCF38C8A5D69203.title": "Protect the workers",
  "quest.3FCF38C8A5D69203.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.3FCF38C8A5D69203.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A larger colony needs guards and coverage near its workplaces. Walls alone do not equip or assign a guard.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a Guard Tower, assign a guard, provide appropriate equipment and inspect patrol/guard settings. Light common paths and keep entrances usable by citizens.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Balance defense with food and production. Citizens' complaints and raid notifications are useful management signals."
  ],
  "task.2E018C6E27723ABD.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.055FBE8444D16357.title": "Recruit deliberately",
  "quest.055FBE8444D16357.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.055FBE8444D16357.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Visitors and new citizens are useful only when you can give them a home, food and a productive role.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a Tavern when ready. Inspect recruitment requirements and citizen skills, then choose a recruit suited to a real vacancy rather than filling every slot immediately.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Read the workplace's skill requirements. A suitable worker is more valuable than the first available name."
  ],
  "task.1D02F69698EF39CF.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.68E68A1EDDCDE2AC.title": "When a citizen stops",
  "quest.68E68A1EDDCDE2AC.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.68E68A1EDDCDE2AC.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Idle animation is not a diagnosis. A citizen may need a tool, recipe, food, research, safe path or a finished building.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Inspect the citizen's status, their hut, open requests and active work order in that order. Fix one cause, wait for the worker to react, and confirm the job advances.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not repeatedly break hut blocks to fix requests. Preserve their assignments and diagnose the missing condition instead."
  ],
  "task.757ABD17CEF8742D.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.1B6DFE41CB364491.title": "Project: supplied expansion",
  "quest.1B6DFE41CB364491.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.1B6DFE41CB364491.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A functioning colony is a repeatable production and delivery system, not merely a collection of completed buildings.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Request one new building. Let your warehouse, couriers and crafters supply several of its materials. Resolve the remaining shortages, finish construction, staff it and explain its role in the colony.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use the same cycle for future expansion: identify a need, plan space, prepare materials, build, staff and verify."
  ]
}
